      {"h":"Workflow pack B. Policy questions desk","text":"Staff send HR the same policy questions every week. Answer them from the policy, with section numbers, and build a staff FAQ.\nMaterial for this pack is below.","files":[{"href":"practice/Sample_Hybrid_Work_Policy.docx","label":"Sample_Hybrid_Work_Policy.docx"},{"href":"practice/HR_Leave_Policy_Extract.txt","label":"HR_Leave_Policy_Extract.txt"}]},
      {"h":"Workflow pack C. Monthly absence report","text":"Turn the monthly absence spreadsheet into a short summary for department managers, with the figures checked.\nMaterial for this pack is below.","files":[{"href":"practice/HR_Absence_Sample.xlsx","label":"HR_Absence_Sample.xlsx"}]},
      {"h":"A · The brief","text":"Need 1 CSR for the contact centre. Handles calls, email and WhatsApp about bills, outages and new connections. Must stay calm with upset customers and be good on a computer. Shift work including some weekends. CXC English and Maths minimum; call centre experience a plus."},
      {"h":"A · Criteria","text":"1. CXC passes in English and Maths\n2. Experience dealing with customers\n3. Comfortable using computer systems\n4. Available for shift work, including weekends\n5. Preferred: call centre experience"},
      {"h":"A · Applicant A","text":"CXC: English Grade II, Mathematics Grade III, Office Administration Grade I. Customer Service Agent, telecoms call centre, 2021 to 2024: billing and fault calls by phone and live chat; logged cases in a CRM ticketing system; highest customer satisfaction score on the team in 2023. Available for rotating shifts."},
      {"h":"A · Applicant B","text":"CXC: English Grade I, Principles of Business Grade II. Cashier, supermarket, 2020 to 2024: handled payments and returns, trained new cashiers. Volunteer, church office: data entry in Excel. Would prefer weekday work."},
      {"h":"A · Applicant C","text":"Associate degree in Business Administration, 2023. CXC: English Grade I, Mathematics Grade II. Administrative assistant, law office, 2023 to now: answers phones, schedules appointments, uses Word and Outlook daily."},
      {"h":"B · The questions","text":"1. Can I work from home two days a week?\n2. Will the company pay for my internet if I work from home?\n3. Can I use ChatGPT at home to help me write customer emails?\n4. If hybrid work doesn't suit me, how do I stop?"},
      {"h":"C · What managers want","text":"Total days absent by department and by reason, any department well above the others, and three plain-English points to discuss. No names: the file uses employee codes."}
